  message: "WORK DONE on branch jgstern-agent/fix/kibah (not merged), commit 5e60e3ea7d.\n\nPremise correction: python's WI-gulot did NOT choose an edge; it chases the alias at the CALL site (function_aliases consumed by _process_call). This branch takes the item's own first design instead (an edge from the variable), because a Go package-level func var is the test seam: what a call reaches is the variable, and its initializer is one value of it. Calls keep binding the variable (INV-nopoh).\n\n_emit_go_alias_edges: for each package-level `var x = <identifier | selector>` naming a repo function, `calls` variable -> target, evidence function_reference (bare names in the caller's package, selectors by operand as WI-kibah resolves them). A call initializer stays INV-nopoh's anchor; a literal or a typed-only var emits nothing. An alias of an OUTSIDE function keeps its module_attr_ref, now anchored on the variable (new `owner_kinds` parameter on core emit_module_attribute_refs / _innermost_callable_at, default unchanged for other languages).\n\nBehavioural evidence: alertmanager test/with_api_v2/mock.go and test/cli/mock.go now emit NewWebhook/Alert/At/Between -> test/testutils functions (8 edges) plus 2 CompareCollectors; cert-manager 2; coredns and prometheus 0. io-boundaries on `var readFile = os.ReadFile; func viaAlias(p string) { readFile(p) }; func main() { viaAlias(\"a\") }`: dev reports the fs_read `<- main.go (main.go:1)` with no entry point; branch `<- readFile (main.go:5)`, reachable from main. module_attr_ref anchors moved file -> variable on 63 / 539 / 253 / 690 sites (alertmanager / coredns / cert-manager / prometheus; includes WI-kugap's shadow drops).\n\nTargeted smart-test on HEAD 5e60e3ea7d: 15728 passed, 5 xfailed, 100% coverage on changed files."  # 8829
